---
// The data flow through FairRootManager in one FairRunAna run: a source fills the input branches,
// the tasks read branches and register new ones, and the sink writes the persistent branches.
// The flag of each registered branch is a switch: the diagram shows if the branch reaches the output file.
// Paths are relative to the FairRoot repository.
//
// The example: examples/advanced/Tutorial3/macro/run_digi_reco_one.C:32-57. One FairRunAna with a
// FairFileSource (data/testrun_<engine>_f0.root), a FairRootFileSink and two tasks, added in this order:
// FairTestDetectorDigiTask, then FairTestDetectorRecoTask. The diagram does not show the file names.
//
// Facts and where they come from:
// - Input tree: run_sim_sep.C (FairRunSim) writes data/testrun_<engine>_f<n>.root (run_sim_sep.C:40-43) and
//   calls SetStoreTraj(kTRUE) (87). FairMCApplication::InitGeometry() calls FairTrajFilter::Init() before
//   RegisterOutput() (fairroot/base/sim/FairMCApplication.cxx:857-862, 875). The registrations, in order, all
//   with kTRUE: "GeoTracks" (fairroot/base/steer/FairTrajFilter.h:119, FairTrajFilter.cxx:78-81); "MCTrack"
//   (examples/common/mcstack/FairStack.cxx:315-322, FairMCApplication.cxx:949; the stack is made in
//   examples/common/gconfig/g3Config.C:27); "FairTestDetectorPoint" (examples/advanced/Tutorial3/simulation/
//   FairTestDetector.cxx:122-131, FairMCApplication.cxx:957-969, only active detectors register); and
//   "MCEventHeader." (fairroot/base/event/FairMCEventHeader.cxx:82-86, FairMCApplication.cxx:977).
//   FairRunSim registers no "EventHeader.". The tested run_sim.C makes the same branches (SetStoreTraj(kTRUE)
//   at 110, FairTestDetector at 90); it feeds run_digi.C and run_reco.C, which run the same two tasks in two runs.
// - Tree and folder names: GetTreeName() is "cbmsim" by default; GetFolderName() is "cbmroot" if the run is
//   not an analysis run, else "cbmout" (fairroot/base/steer/FairRootManager.cxx:932-961; both can come from
//   rootmanager.dat, 898-930). FairRunAna sets fAna = kTRUE (fairroot/base/steer/FairRunAna.cxx:88), FairRun
//   starts with kFALSE (FairRun.cxx:49). So the input file has the folder cbmroot and the output file the folder
//   cbmout. FairFileSource looks for GetFolderName(), then "cbmroot", then "cbmout"
//   (fairroot/base/source/FairFileSource.cxx:164-175). The sink writes the folder and the tree with
//   GetFolderName() and GetTreeName() (fairroot/base/sink/FairRootFileSink.cxx:242-245).
// - FairRunAna::Init(): InitSource(), InitSink() (FairRunAna.cxx:142-143). The run registers its event header:
//   evtHeader->Register(GetSink() ? fStoreEventHeader : false) (FairRunAna.cxx:194 or 204), which is
//   Register("EventHeader.", "EvtHeader", this, ...) (fairroot/base/event/FairEventHeader.cxx:17-20).
//   fStoreEventHeader is kTRUE (FairRunAna.cxx:85); SetEventHeaderPersistence() changes it (FairRunAna.h:70).
//   Then fTask->InitTask() (238), then WriteFolder() (250). FairTrajFilter::Init() runs only if a filter exists
//   (FairRunAna.cxx:241-244, FairTrajFilter.cxx:32); the macro makes none, so the output has no GeoTracks.
// - Tasks: FairRun::AddTask() adds to the main task (FairRun.cxx:110-114). InitTask() and ExecuteTasks()
//   go through the tasks in list order (fairroot/base/steer/FairTask.cxx:49-64, 128-168, 170-208).
//   FairTestDetectorDigiTask::Init(): GetObject("FairTestDetectorPoint"), then
//   Register("FairTestDetectorDigi", "FairTestDetector", fDigiArray, kTRUE)
//   (examples/advanced/Tutorial3/digitization/FairTestDetectorDigiTask.cxx:39, 48).
//   FairTestDetectorRecoTask::Init(): GetObject("FairTestDetectorDigi"), then
//   Register("FairTestDetectorHit", "FairTestDetector", fHitArray, kTRUE)
//   (examples/advanced/Tutorial3/reconstruction/FairTestDetectorRecoTask.cxx:44, 52).
// - GetObject() looks in the memory map first, then in the folders of the input file, and lets the source
//   connect the branch; then the object is in the memory map (FairRootManager.cxx:486-495, 723-753;
//   FairFileSource::ActivateObject() sets the branch address, FairFileSource.cxx:538-550). So a branch that a
//   task registers with kFALSE is still in memory, and a later task gets it with GetObject(). Only the input
//   branches that a task asks for get into the memory map. The source itself connects "MCEventHeader." to
//   fill the event header of the run (FairFileSource.cxx:255-265, 700-712).
// - Register() -> RegisterImpl(): with kTRUE, the object goes to the sink; always, it goes to the memory map and
//   the branch list (FairRootManager.cxx:148-178). FairRootFileSink::RegisterImpl() puts it into a subfolder
//   of the output folder (FairRootFileSink.cxx:214-226), which InitSink() makes (78-98,
//   FairRootManager.cxx:378-381). RegisterAny() and InitObjectAs() follow the same model
//   (fairroot/base/steer/FairRootManager.h:452-466, 471-515); Tutorial3 uses Register() and GetObject().
// - WriteFolder() makes the output tree: new TTree(GetTreeName(), "/<folder name>", 99)
//   (FairRootFileSink.cxx:238-249). In ROOT, a title that starts with "/" makes one branch for each object
//   in that folder (ROOT tree/tree/src/TTree.cxx: TTree::TTree() calls TTree::Branch(const char* foldername,
//   ...)); TruncateBranchNames() cuts the names to the object names (FairRootFileSink.cxx:100-175). Branches of
//   RegisterAny() come from CreatePersistentBranchesAny() (261-289). So the output tree has only the branches
//   registered with kTRUE: EventHeader., FairTestDetectorDigi, FairTestDetectorHit, in this order (folder
//   order: EvtHeader first, because the run registers it before InitTask()).
// - Input branches: FairFileSource::Init() adds the input folder to the list of input folders and the input
//   names to the branch list (FairFileSource.cxx:189-212), not to the output folder. So the sink does not copy
//   them. (Their names are in the BranchList object of the output file, FairRootManager.cxx:383-390.)
// - Each event, FairRunAna::Run() calls ReadEvent(i), FillEventHeader(), ExecuteTask(""), Fill()
//   (FairRunAna.cxx:313-327). ReadEvent(i) -> FairFileSource::ReadEvent() -> fInChain->GetEntry(i)
//   (FairRootManager.cxx:409-431, FairFileSource.cxx:290-298). FillEventHeader() lets the source fill the
//   event header of the run, the object registered as "EventHeader." (FairRunAna.cxx:321, FairRun.cxx:162-168,
//   241-249, FairFileSource.cxx:700-712). ReadEvent(i) fills only the private header of the manager
//   (FairRootManager.cxx:89, 425), so the diagram fills "EventHeader." in the FillEventHeader() step.
//   ExecuteTask("") calls Exec() of each active task in order. Fill() -> FairRootManager::Fill() ->
//   FairRootFileSink::Fill() -> fOutTree->Fill() (FairRunAna.cxx:617-624, FairRootManager.cxx:331-335,
//   FairRootFileSink.cxx:302-309).

type P = [number, number];
type Reg = 'eh' | 'dg' | 'ht';
type Key = Reg | 'pt';
interface T {
  x: number;
  y: number;
}
interface Layout {
  id: 'wide' | 'narrow';
  W: number;
  H: number;
  lanes: (T & { t: string })[];
  src: { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number; title: T; sub: (T & { t: string })[]; ent: (T & { n: string; port?: boolean })[] };
  snk: { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number; title: T; sub: (T & { t: string })[]; ent: Record<Reg, T> };
  mgr: { title: T; sub: T };
  chipW: number;
  chips: Record<Key, P>;
  taskW: number;
  tasks: [P, P];
  arrows: { x: number; y1: number; y2: number; t: string; reg?: Reg }[];
  read: P[];
  flagX: number;
  skip: T; // "not copied", on the row of the input branch
  cw: number; // width of one character of the names (JetBrains Mono: 0.6 em)
  post: Record<Reg, P[]>;
  stop: Record<Reg, P>;
  rails?: { d: string; on: Reg[] }[];
  loop: { label: T; steps: (T & { t: string; more?: string })[]; rail: string; dir: 'v' | 'h' };
  toks: Record<string, P[]>;
}

const CH = 22; // chip height
const TH = 26; // task height
const FW = 56; // flag width
const FH = 20; // flag height
const NAMES: Record<Key, string> = {
  eh: 'EventHeader.',
  pt: 'FairTestDetectorPoint',
  dg: 'FairTestDetectorDigi',
  ht: 'FairTestDetectorHit',
};
const TASKS = ['FairTestDetectorDigiTask', 'FairTestDetectorRecoTask'];
const REG: Reg[] = ['eh', 'dg', 'ht'];
const cy = (L: Layout, k: Key) => L.chips[k][1] + CH / 2;

// Wide: input file | FairRootManager and the tasks | output file. The rows of a branch line up.
const wide: Layout = {
  id: 'wide',
  W: 660,
  H: 344,
  lanes: [
    { t: 'INPUT FILE', x: 0, y: 12 },
    { t: 'OUTPUT FILE', x: 480, y: 12 },
